summary:
- topic: FY25 Budget Presentation
  text: The Superintendent presented the final FY25 Superintendent’sBudget, highlighting
    a 5% school operating budget increase and a 3.82% mill rate increase. He noted
    these figures are competitive and fair to taxpayers, especially when compared
    to proposed increases in neighboring school districts.
- topic: Budget Challenges and Priorities
  text: Key challenges in this budget cycle included enrollment variability, the loss
    of federal COVID-19 funds which supported 19 positions, and rising fixed costs.
    The administration focused on preserving excellence and fostering equity while
    navigating these constraints.
- topic: Extended Learning Opportunities (ELO) Program Update
  text: The ELO program will continue at SOUTHPORTLANDHIGHSCHOOL through a new partnership
    with JMG. A JMG staff member will serve as a full-time "ELO Navigator," ensuring
    the program's continuation and aligning it with broader career-connected education
    goals after a two-year grant expired.
- topic: Athletics Program Equity Discussion
  text: Board members discussed equity in athletics, focusing on removing financial
    barriers to participation. The conversation covered admission fees for events
    and the cost of sports-specific items, with a consensus that essential uniform
    items, such as swimsuits, should be provided by the district.
- topic: Unfunded Positions Review
  text: The Board inquired about the costs of several requested but unfunded positions
    in the FY25 budget. The administration provided estimates, including $100,000
    for a Director of Intervention and Mental Health and $175,000 for an additional
    pre-K classroom, should funds become available later.
- topic: FY25 Budget and School Calendar Approval
  text: Following discussion, the Board of Education voted unanimously to approve
    the FY25Superintendent’sBudget. They also unanimously approved a revision to the
    2024-2025school year calendar, extending the school year by one day to June 13,
    2025.
